  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nuweiba Gen Z</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is aiming at preserving, transmitting and promoting Sinai&#x2019;s Bedouin cultural heritage by contributing to cultural diversity and dialogue between the local Egyptian Bedouin communities and the rest of the Egyptian society. The project contributes to the inclusion and empowerment of women from the local Bedouin community by guaranteeing that a substantial number of the participants in all the activities are women, and focusing on capacity building and transmission of knowledge between women. The female co-founder of Dayra serves as a role model in this regard. As the project is carried out in an area that traditionally does not allow women presence outside of the household, the inclusion of women in the project activities is made possible by already existing networks between Dayra and the local community.</narrative>
  </description>
